  "body": "### Summary\nAs a respondent, I want to see each scenario concretely, so that I choose without guessing.\n\n### Scope\n- Theme 1: \"pages améliorées\" mock-up, limited to improvements possible with the WebView; short GIF for \"lecture continue\".\n- Theme 2: two new layouts on iPad and unfolded Duo, next to the current screenshot; cards of the sidebar sections for the card sort.\n- Same topic, theme and device as the UX-07 screenshots; Apple HIG and the \"room for content\" guideline; no proposal classed Non visible.\n\n### Deliverable\n`docs/ux/questionnaire/visuels/scenarios/`.\n\n### Blocked by\n\n- #631\n\n### Model and review\nOpus on the Mac, Fable review, PO validation. Brief: `docs/ux/cadrage-agents-questionnaire.md` §3, UX-08.\n\nTracked on #628.\n\n### Before you start\n\nRead, in order: `AGENTS.md`, `docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md`, `docs/agents/LESSONS.md`, then `docs/ux/README.md`. The UX documents are in French. Until the docs PR is merged into `dev-swift`, read them on branch `docs/ux-questionnaire`.\n\nRules: no proposal the PO classed **Non** may appear in the survey (`docs/ux/tri-m5-decisions.md` §3.5 and §4.7). The reader keeps the WebView: the survey only shows improvements possible with it. Stop and report if an instruction contradicts the plan.\n\n---\n_Opened with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code) for the PO (Bruno), 2026-11-07._\n\n\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
